  "family": {
    "id": "polynomial-multiplication-baselines",
    "issue": "c7113c5a",
    "purpose": "kernel-family",
    "description": "Current-code gf2 against pinned gf2x 1.3.0 (gf2x_mul_r), both built for the native host, for the gf2 operations whose unreduced stage has a gf2x form. Equivalent cells: the unreduced long product in GF(2)[x] through the dispatched wide kernels a Gf2mWide consumer reaches (4 and 9 words) and through the scalar schoolbook (64, 256 and 2048 words, and the public clmul_wide_slice API at 4 words), warm and streaming, on 1, 6, 12 and 24 CPUs. Internal baselines, labelled internal-: the raw batch of 1024 independent 64x64 products and the whole-consumer GF(2^8) dot product, whose gf2x arm is a composed, non-equivalent reference of 1024 gf2x_mul_r calls. Field reduction is excluded from every timed long product and reported separately. This is the protocol-v3 attempt at the question the protocol-v1 confirmation confirmation-c7113c5a-20260907t194909z answered; the family ledger carries that reservation. Every cell is a comparator gap with gf2x as candidate, so a speedup below one means gf2 is faster. The survey adopts nothing, adds no gf2x production dependency and changes no gf2 multiplication algorithm."
  },
  "frozen": {
    "frozen_utc": "2026-09-10T16:54:02Z"
  },
  "effect": {
    "worthwhile_speedup": null,
    "rationale": "This family declares no improvement cell: every cell compares current gf2 with an external comparator and the issue excludes adoption, so no worthwhile-speedup threshold applies.",
    "measurement_resolution": 0.24,
    "resolution_evidence": {
      "receipt": "dev/bench_results/c7113c5a/v3-r1-baselines-pilot/receipt.json",
      "sha256": "f8d260031b5357a40bac00e324fc875f8a6bbec72d6c248188fe17ab43c8aae1"
    },
    "equivalence_margin": 1.25,
    "equivalence_rationale": "This family's pilot-derived measurement resolution is 0.24, set by the twelve-core cell, and protocol v3 requires every margin to exceed one plus it. A 25 percent band is the smallest two-decimal margin above that bound; within it a consumer choosing between the libraries still decides on portability and licensing (gf2x is GPL-3.0-or-later, gf2 is MIT) rather than on speed. It replaces the pilot addendum's 1.15, which that resolution invalidates.",
    "material_gap_threshold": 1.25,
    "material_gap_rationale": "A quarter of the runtime is the smallest gap that survives the adapter and conversion costs a consumer pays to reach an external library, so it is the smallest gap that would change an engineering decision about the gf2 path. The confirmation freezes a pilot-derived measurement resolution strictly below this threshold."
  },
